A||N||5||Calab52||Torsion Rod Help!!!!!||||5||
Z||000000||Calab52||09-26-2001||04:42 PM||||I have an 87GT with a wing on my decklid. The torsion rods are the wrong color, red instead of white. I am replacing them now with the right rod, except we cant get the bolt that goes from the hingr to the decklid in because the bar is over the hole. The red torsion bar the bar only covers the hole a litte, but this one covers it completely. Does any body have any suggestions or have had the same problem? Please let me know...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Calab52||09-26-2001||07:33 PM||||Is there anybody out there that can help???||||reg||1
Z||000002||foxgapfiero||09-26-2001||10:15 PM||||Are you sure you have the correct torsion rod? All the ones I have are black and the only thing that is different is the thickness of the rod. You know thin ones for no wing thick ones with wing. The last time I did one  it was difficult but the pin did finally slide in the hinge support. Do you have a manual?  The procedure is explained pretty thourgh in there. Be careful not to let the hinge snap back it will break the rear window. <P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000003||Calab52||09-26-2001||10:29 PM||||The rods are color coded, red with no wing and white with wing. The white is definitly thicker, it just seems to cover where the bolt goes in the hinge and decklid area making it no close correctly.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bazooka||09-27-2001||05:05 PM||||Caleb,<BR>   I've always used a large slotted screwdriver to assist the rod into position into the hinge bracket slot. Once it in there you should apply the tension to it by prying the torsion rod downward just under the bracket with a 3 foot prybar. Then the 4 inch pin can be slipped in thru one of the three holes made for the needed tension. If the torsion rod still interferes with the locator pin then you may not have seated the rod properly or you still need to pry the rod downward at the bracket until there is enough clearance for the pin.<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <P>*******************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Calab52:<BR><B>The rods are color coded, red with no wing and white with wing. The white is definitly thicker, it just seems to cover where the bolt goes in the hinge and decklid area making it no close correctly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*******************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-27-2001||06:56 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A> <P>$69bux, and it's awesome.<P>Get rid of the torsionn rods alltogether, and never loose a finger to them again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
